{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"5484ff14-c76b-4fb4-9a8a-8e498a3a500b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause and fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-w7iVCC/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary\n\n1. **Why the second publish returned 500**:\n   - On the first publish, the DynamoDB table was empty. No related stories were scored, leaving `similar: []`.\n   - On the second publish, `related()` evaluated similarity against existing items. In [`similarity()`](file:///private/tmp/h-w7iVCC/src/app.py#L25-L32), the computed score was returned as a Python `float`. Boto3 rejects `float` attributes with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`, causing `handler()` to log an error and return 500.\n\n2. **Fix applied**:\n   - In [`src/app.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-w7iVCC/src/app.py#L32), converted the similarity return value to `Decimal(str(round(...)))`.\n   - In [`tests/test_publish.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-w7iVCC/tests/test_publish.py#L26-L59), added unit and handler tests for second/subsequent writes to ensure regression testing exercises populated-table paths.\n","duration_seconds":70.573912,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":126874,"output_tokens":3256,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":245694,"total_tokens":130130}}}
